{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.55,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["T4"],
      "pins": ["T4.1", "T4.2", "T4.3"],
      "nets": ["ATO_VALVE", "NET0032", "NET0035"],
      "obs": "On sheet 1 the ATO-Valve low-side switch T4 is populated with an AO3400A (a 30 V, SOT‑23 N‑MOSFET), gate driven from NET0032 through R17 (100 Ω) and pre‑driven by T1 (BT3904). The 60 V‑class AON6407 that the spec assigns to this position instead appears at the 24 V input reverse‑polarity circuit (T6).",
      "exp": "Spec §2 states: \"T3 — AON6407 (8‑DFN N‑MOSFET) | ATO solenoid‑valve low‑side switch ... drives ATO_VALVE net; gate driven through R10 (100 Ω), pre‑driven via T4 (BT3904).\" The valve switch must be the AON6407, not the 30 V AO3400A.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Sheet 1, 'ATO Valve' block: MOSFET symbol labelled \"T4 AO3400A\" with R17 100Ω on its gate and D6 SS34 flyback on the +24 V solenoid node."},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "T3 — AON6407 (8-DFN N-MOSFET) | ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch ... drives ATO_VALVE net; gate driven through R10 (100 Ω), pre-driven via T4 (BT3904)."}
      ],
      "impact": "The ATO valve MOSFET is a 30 V‑rated part switching a 24 V inductive solenoid. With only ~6 V of Vds headroom, the SMBJ28A input clamp (≈45 V surge clamp) or supply overshoot can exceed the AO3400A's Vds rating and destroy the valve switch; the 8‑DFN footprint called out for the AON6407 is also not what is drawn.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    },
    {
      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["PR4", "H12"],
      "pins": ["PR4.VCC", "PR4.SCL", "PR4.SDA", "PR4.GND"],
      "nets": ["NET0006", "NET0007", "+5V"],
      "obs": "On sheet 1 the TF‑Luna LiDAR PR4 is wired: VCC→+5 V, SCL→NET0007, SDA→NET0006 (the main non‑isolated I2C bus, the same nets carried by the R42/R54 2.2 kΩ pull‑ups and the ESP32 IO4/IO5), through header H12.",
      "exp": "Spec §4.3/§6 state the LiDAR is schematic documentation only: \"the r2 netlist shows PR1 with on_board: no ... and all four pins (VCC, SDA, SCL, GND) typed free — i.e., it is not connected to any net in this design.\"",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Sheet 1, 'Water Height Sensor': PR4 LiDAR pins SCL/SDA joined to NET0007/NET0006 via H12, VCC to +5 V."},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "all four pins (VCC, SDA, SCL, GND) typed free — i.e., it is not connected to any net in this design."}
      ],
      "impact": "An I2C device the intended design deliberately left unconnected is now bridged onto the main I2C bus; if a TF‑Luna is plugged into H12 it appears as an unmanaged slave and adds bus loading/capacitance, contrary to the architecture (water level is meant to be sensed by the float switches, not the LiDAR).",
      "confidence": 0.45
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing deviates from the intended r2 design in two places: the ATO‑valve low‑side switch is built with a 30 V AO3400A instead of the spec‑mandated AON6407 (insufficient Vds headroom on a 24 V inductive load), and the TF‑Luna LiDAR, which the spec says must be left unwired with free pins, is in fact tied onto the main I2C bus via H12."
}

